{"tool_name":"pdbe-kb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"pdbe-kb","home":"https://pdbe-kb.org","summary":"Protein Data Bank in Europe - Knowledge Base","addition_date":"2022-04-09T10:28:37.967833Z","last_update_date":"2022-04-09T10:28:37.970519Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:pdbe-kb","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"PDBe-KB consortium","typeEntity":"Consortium"}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/download/api/docs"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/PDBe-KB/pdbe-kb-manual"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/PDBe-KB/pdbe-kb-manual/wiki"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Aggregation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3436"},{"term":"Deposition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3431"},{"term":"PTM site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0417"},{"term":"Parsing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_1812"},{"term":"Small molecule design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_4009"}]}],"name":"PDBe-KB","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/NAR/GKAB988","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author(s) 2021.The Protein Data Bank in Europe \u2013 Knowledge Base (PDBe-KB, https://pdbe-kb.org) is an open collaboration between world-leading specialist data resources contributing functional and biophysical annotations derived from or relevant to the Protein Data Bank (PDB). The goal of PDBe-KB is to place macromolecular structure data in their biological context by developing standardised data exchange formats and integrating functional annotations from the contributing partner resources into a knowledge graph that can provide valuable biological insights. Since we described PDBe-KB in 2019, there have been significant improvements in the variety of available annotation data sets and user functionality. Here, we provide an overview of the consortium, highlighting the addition of annotations such as predicted covalent binders, phosphorylation sites, effects of mutations on the protein structure and energetic local frustration. In addition, we describe a library of reusable web-based visualisation components and introduce new features such as a bulk download data service and a novel superposition service that generates clusters of superposed protein chains weekly for the whole PDB archive.","authors":[{"name":"Al-Lazikani B."},{"name":"Andreini C."},{"name":"Anyango S."},{"name":"Armstrong D."},{"name":"Barton G.J."},{"name":"Bednar D."},{"name":"Berka K."},{"name":"Berrisford J."},{"name":"Blundell T."},{"name":"Brock K.P."},{"name":"Carazo J.M."},{"name":"Choudhary P."},{"name":"Damborsky J."},{"name":"David A."},{"name":"Deshpande M."},{"name":"Dey S."},{"name":"Dunbrack R."},{"name":"Fraternali F."},{"name":"Gibson T."},{"name":"Helmer-Citterich M."},{"name":"Hoksza D."},{"name":"Hopf T."},{"name":"Jakubec D."},{"name":"Kannan N."},{"name":"Krivak R."},{"name":"Kumar M."},{"name":"Levy E.D."},{"name":"London N."},{"name":"Macias J.R."},{"name":"Marks D.S."},{"name":"Martens L."},{"name":"McGowan S.A."},{"name":"McGreig J.E."},{"name":"Modi V."},{"name":"Nadzirin N."},{"name":"Nair S.S."},{"name":"Orengo C."},{"name":"Parra R.G."},{"name":"Pepe G."},{"name":"Piovesan D."},{"name":"Pravda L."},{"name":"Prilusky J."},{"name":"Putignano V."},{"name":"Radusky L.G."},{"name":"Ramasamy P."},{"name":"Rausch A.O."},{"name":"Recio J.F."},{"name":"Reuter N."},{"name":"Rodriguez L.A."},{"name":"Rollins N.J."},{"name":"Rosato A."},{"name":"Rubach P."},{"name":"Serrano L."},{"name":"Singh G."},{"name":"Skoda P."},{"name":"Sorzano C.O.S."},{"name":"Srivatsan M.M."},{"name":"Sternberg M."},{"name":"Stourac J."},{"name":"Sulkowska J.I."},{"name":"Svobodova R."},{"name":"Tanweer A."},{"name":"Thornton J."},{"name":